      "dom_id": "question-132483",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "On a webpage, visitors arrive continuously in time, independently, and at a constant average rate of one every $15$ seconds.  Determine the probability of waiting for the next visitor for less than $0.5$ minutes.  Round your answer to $4$ decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "Since visitors arrive continuously in time, independently, and at a constant average rate, we can model the time until the next visitor appears using an exponential distribution.\n\nAn exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the time between two consecutive visitor arrivals. Since visitors arrive on average every $15$ seconds, the rate is $\\lambda =60÷15=4$ visitors per minute.\n\nThe time between two consecutive visitor arrivals can be modeled as an exponential random variable with rate $\\lambda =4,$ and we can write \n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(4).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}4{e}^{-4x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability of waiting for the next visitor for less than \n$0.5$ minutes is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<0.5) & ={\\int }_{0}^{0.5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{0.5}4{e}^{-4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-4x}{|}_{0}^{0.5} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2}+{e}^{0} \\\\  & ≈0.8647\\end{aligned}\n$$",
